  "introduction": "Consolidate primary mathematics and prepare for secondary study through reverse percentages and percentage change.",
  "definition": "When a value changes by a decimal rate r, the new value equals original × (1+r) for an increase or original × (1−r) for a decrease. To recover the original, divide the new value by the corresponding nonzero multiplier. Successive changes multiply their factors.",
